{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The ReadIndex interface explicitly permits dropped requests and assigns retries to callers, so the deferred-read hook difference does not yet establish a client-completion violation.\n\nA separate safety question is worth checking: the singleton ReadIndex fast path bypasses the current-term commitment guard. I’ll inspect whether restart can legally leave the durable log ahead of the restored commit index, making that shortcut return an index below a previously completed write.\n"}}
